WEBVTT

00:01.335 --> 00:03.337
[♪ theme music playing]

00:29.112 --> 00:30.197
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

00:33.283 --> 00:34.826
CHARACTERS, EVENTS, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND PLACES IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

00:34.910 --> 00:36.203
ALL CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS
FILMED IN A SAFE ENVIRONMENT

00:36.286 --> 00:37.287
[Haran] Huh?

00:37.371 --> 00:39.039
EPISODE 11

00:39.623 --> 00:40.624
[chuckles softly]

00:55.138 --> 00:57.975
THANKS FOR THE

01:14.241 --> 01:16.076
[♪ dramatic music playing]

01:16.159 --> 01:17.411
Kang Hyeokchan…

01:17.494 --> 01:19.663
KANG HYEOKCHAN
GLASS TUBE

01:20.455 --> 01:22.624
Why is this name here?

01:27.045 --> 01:29.047
Hospitalized? Hyeokchan?

01:29.131 --> 01:30.924
He hurt his hand badly in the lab.

01:31.008 --> 01:32.384
He even got surgery.

01:33.218 --> 01:36.096
How does he know Hyeokchan?

01:38.307 --> 01:39.975
OUTSIDE THE LAB

01:40.517 --> 01:42.060
"Lab"?

01:42.686 --> 01:43.854
[Chan] NaClO.

01:43.937 --> 01:45.272
Sodium hypochlorite…

01:45.355 --> 01:46.940
[officer] I guess
you majored in that field.

01:47.024 --> 01:49.276
It seems like you majored
in engineering, not art.

01:52.988 --> 01:54.197
Huh?

01:54.281 --> 01:55.449
This is…

01:56.366 --> 01:59.536
[Sujin] I'm only visiting, so I'm not
authorized to treat patients directly.

01:59.619 --> 02:00.746
I came from Boston.

02:02.539 --> 02:03.540
[stutters] Boston?

02:04.916 --> 02:06.084
[sighs]

02:09.338 --> 02:11.048
[Seok] There was
an international conference.

02:11.131 --> 02:12.466
Your school…

02:12.924 --> 02:16.678
-No, your former school…
-[Chan] That's enough.

02:22.100 --> 02:23.602
Boston Institute of Technology.

02:31.068 --> 02:33.278
[♪ soft emotional music playing]

02:35.072 --> 02:36.073
[Genius huffs]

02:36.740 --> 02:37.741
Ah.

02:39.493 --> 02:40.535
[sighs]

02:41.662 --> 02:42.663
Is she upstairs?

02:45.040 --> 02:46.625
THANKS FOR THE

02:48.502 --> 02:51.129
-[line connects, ringing]
-[inhales sharply]

02:57.260 --> 02:58.261
[♪ music fades]

03:05.477 --> 03:07.813
[♪ tense music playing]

03:13.026 --> 03:14.695
KANG HYEOKCHAN, GLASS TUBE, BLOOD

03:14.778 --> 03:17.239
KANG HYEOKCHAN HOSPITALIZED, WOMAN
THAT SOUND WAS HER BRACELET

03:27.416 --> 03:29.334
[exhales shakily] No…

03:39.219 --> 03:40.637
[Hyeokchan]
Let me tell you something cool.

03:40.720 --> 03:43.348
My dorm roommate is Korean,
and his name's Chan, too.

03:43.432 --> 03:45.517
[Hayeong] You used to call him Chan.

03:45.600 --> 03:47.561
Your old boyfriend, Hyeokchan.

03:48.270 --> 03:49.396
Hyeokchan's roommate

03:50.397 --> 03:53.608
was Seonu Chan?

03:53.692 --> 03:54.901
[vibrating]

03:54.985 --> 03:56.486
SEONU CHAN

03:57.863 --> 03:58.864
[Chan] Watch out!

03:58.947 --> 04:00.073
Song Haran!

04:01.074 --> 04:03.118
[Haran] I met you for the first time
a few days ago.

04:03.201 --> 04:05.078
How long have you known me?

04:05.579 --> 04:07.956
Tell me how you know me.

04:08.039 --> 04:09.583
What are you hiding?

04:12.294 --> 04:13.503
He's known me

04:14.880 --> 04:16.089
for seven years.

04:19.176 --> 04:20.302
[door closes]

04:25.932 --> 04:26.933
[♪ music fades]

04:30.270 --> 04:32.272
[♪ somber music playing]

04:39.654 --> 04:41.239
[Haran] He knew my face

04:42.199 --> 04:44.075
and my name.

04:45.285 --> 04:46.411
It's nice to meet you.

04:46.495 --> 04:47.496
Ah…

04:48.330 --> 04:49.498
It's nice to meet you.

04:50.165 --> 04:53.460
I saw you up close earlier,
looking at the Sisley painting.

04:55.086 --> 04:56.254
No…

04:56.838 --> 04:58.507
This can't be right. No.

04:59.216 --> 05:00.217
No…

05:00.300 --> 05:01.802
Hey, it smells like rain.

05:01.885 --> 05:04.137
[Chan] That's the smell
of organic matter diffusing.

05:04.221 --> 05:05.472
Petrichor.

05:05.555 --> 05:08.266
[Haran] There's another guy
who speaks like him.

05:09.017 --> 05:10.602
She doesn't like eggplants.

05:10.685 --> 05:12.479
[Haran] How do you know
I don't like eggplants?

05:12.562 --> 05:14.272
Yuck. The taste of neon alien.

05:14.356 --> 05:15.607
I'll eat those for you.

05:16.149 --> 05:17.234
The neon aliens.

05:18.860 --> 05:19.945
Then…

05:21.279 --> 05:22.531
all those messages…

05:23.949 --> 05:25.617
were him pretending to be Hyeokchan?

05:31.832 --> 05:33.124
[exhales shakily]

05:33.208 --> 05:34.209
No…

05:35.252 --> 05:37.128
That can't be. No.

05:37.212 --> 05:38.338
He'll explain everything.

05:38.421 --> 05:39.631
No…

05:39.714 --> 05:40.966
This doesn't make sense.

05:41.049 --> 05:42.467
[♪ music continues]

05:56.731 --> 05:58.275
-[cell phone vibrates]
-[Chan] Let's meet.

05:58.358 --> 05:59.526
Let's meet up and talk.

05:59.609 --> 06:00.986
I'll explain everything.

06:05.490 --> 06:06.825
No, please…

06:07.325 --> 06:08.326
Please.

06:08.910 --> 06:09.911
Please…

06:21.047 --> 06:23.675
It must have gotten mixed up
in my stuff back then.

06:24.467 --> 06:26.469
Just consider this pen

06:26.553 --> 06:27.596
a pen that I found for you.

06:30.348 --> 06:32.767
I think you owe me an explanation.

06:32.851 --> 06:34.477
I bought the same pen…

06:37.355 --> 06:38.815
when I was in the States.

06:39.816 --> 06:41.026
Then this pen…

06:42.569 --> 06:44.321
He knew everything…

06:47.407 --> 06:48.742
[breath trembling]

06:58.418 --> 06:59.836
[sighs]

07:01.963 --> 07:02.964
[♪ music fades]

07:13.141 --> 07:14.643
-Hey…
-[Haran] Don't come any closer.

07:23.777 --> 07:25.362
Boston Institute of Technology.

07:26.154 --> 07:27.572
Kang Hyeokchan's roommate.

07:28.615 --> 07:29.908
Have you really known me

07:31.076 --> 07:32.452
for seven years?

07:36.373 --> 07:37.791
[breathes shakily]

07:38.958 --> 07:40.627
-Song Haran.
-Don't say my name.

07:41.127 --> 07:42.170
[breath trembling]

07:42.253 --> 07:43.338
Did you have fun

07:44.172 --> 07:45.799
pretending to be Kang Hyeokchan?

07:45.882 --> 07:47.092
[breath trembling]

07:52.305 --> 07:53.682
Seonu Chan,

07:54.683 --> 07:55.767
who are you?

07:56.476 --> 07:58.478
[high-pitched ringing]

08:01.648 --> 08:03.108
The Seonu Chan

08:03.191 --> 08:05.902
I liked and trusted
until just a few hours ago…

08:05.985 --> 08:07.487
Who is he, really?

08:09.948 --> 08:11.491
[yells] Who are you?

08:11.574 --> 08:13.076
[♪ emotional music playing]

08:13.159 --> 08:14.577
[stutters]

08:15.036 --> 08:16.329
I'm sorry.

08:16.871 --> 08:19.207
I shouldn't have let you
find out like this.

08:19.749 --> 08:21.042
I should've told you…

08:21.126 --> 08:23.795
No wonder you were so flustered
in front of the doctor.

08:24.504 --> 08:26.214
You didn't want to get caught,

08:27.340 --> 08:29.759
because she knew you were in Boston.

08:30.677 --> 08:32.178
Because I couldn't find out.

08:32.887 --> 08:34.889
-I'll explain everything.
-Tell me.

08:36.182 --> 08:37.350
Did you message me

08:38.059 --> 08:40.145
seven years ago,
pretending to be Hyeokchan?

08:40.812 --> 08:41.980
Is that true?

08:45.984 --> 08:46.985
Answer me.

08:49.112 --> 08:52.782
Did you really deceive me
and pretend to be Hyeokchan

08:53.950 --> 08:55.118
behind his back?

08:59.748 --> 09:00.749
I'm sorry.

09:02.417 --> 09:03.418
[breath trembling]

09:04.419 --> 09:05.420
Why?

09:07.422 --> 09:08.465
Why did you do that?

09:11.509 --> 09:12.510
Our laptops

09:13.595 --> 09:15.764
got switched once.

09:15.847 --> 09:16.931
[sighs in disbelief]

09:18.600 --> 09:19.684
[exhales shakily]

09:20.977 --> 09:23.063
Did you have fun
chatting with me like that?

09:23.980 --> 09:26.941
Did you build some kind of fantasy
and start liking me?

09:27.025 --> 09:29.402
I can't even tell
which was really Hyeokchan or you…

09:38.369 --> 09:39.370
The pen.

09:41.998 --> 09:42.999
The engraving.

09:45.210 --> 09:46.211
Who was it?

09:46.711 --> 09:48.379
Was it you or Hyeokchan?

09:53.218 --> 09:55.220
-I'm sorry.
-[exhales shakily]

09:57.305 --> 09:58.306
If that's fake…

09:59.682 --> 10:01.559
[sobbing] Even if this pen is fake…

10:02.435 --> 10:04.979
Then what was I holding onto
the past seven years?

10:06.106 --> 10:08.733
I even hurt my grandma
because of all that.

10:08.817 --> 10:09.818
Why…

10:11.611 --> 10:13.530
You should've at least told me

10:14.572 --> 10:16.783
when you gave me this pen.

10:16.866 --> 10:21.329
When I believed you like a fool,
you should've told me the truth.

10:21.412 --> 10:22.622
I needed time.

10:23.498 --> 10:24.582
My memories aren't…

10:27.418 --> 10:28.503
[sighs exasperatedly]

10:29.295 --> 10:30.296
I'm sorry.

10:31.464 --> 10:32.465
It's all my fault.

10:32.549 --> 10:35.218
Do you even know what it meant
for me to hold your hand?

10:35.301 --> 10:37.345
To open my heart to you?

10:37.428 --> 10:39.514
[sighs] How could you, of all people…

10:39.597 --> 10:41.641
How could you, Seonu Chan?

10:42.392 --> 10:43.518
[sighs dejectedly]

10:44.769 --> 10:47.689
I'm really sorry I hurt you
by making you find out like this.

10:49.107 --> 10:51.192
I won't ask you
to believe everything I say,

10:51.276 --> 10:52.360
so please…

10:52.443 --> 10:56.281
I was surprised that there was someone
who believed in me this much.

10:57.532 --> 10:58.533
I was grateful.

10:59.909 --> 11:01.828
But you knew me all along.

11:02.871 --> 11:04.372
You knew what hurt me the most

11:04.873 --> 11:06.875
and what would break me the easiest.

11:08.209 --> 11:09.294
I thought…

11:12.922 --> 11:14.591
you were like a miracle to me.

11:16.759 --> 11:18.303
But to you…

11:20.263 --> 11:22.098
I was just an experiment.

11:24.642 --> 11:25.894
[Chan sighs dejectedly]

11:26.936 --> 11:28.146
It's not…

11:29.981 --> 11:31.107
No…

11:33.610 --> 11:34.611
[♪ music fades]

11:34.694 --> 11:36.154
Haran, that's not true.

11:36.237 --> 11:37.488
Never.

11:37.989 --> 11:40.617
If you were fake,
you shouldn't have made me like you.

11:41.201 --> 11:43.578
You shouldn't have made me
trust you this much!

11:46.873 --> 11:48.791
I didn't even know it was all fake,

11:48.875 --> 11:50.627
and I foolishly laughed, cried,

11:50.710 --> 11:53.338
and was happy because of you.

11:53.421 --> 11:55.423
[Haran sobbing]

11:56.007 --> 11:59.344
It must have been so fun watching me.

12:00.178 --> 12:01.554
Like a spring picnic.

12:12.106 --> 12:13.107
[Chan pants]

12:13.733 --> 12:15.109
Wait.

12:16.486 --> 12:17.654
Please.

12:17.737 --> 12:20.990
[panting] Please, let me explain.

12:21.074 --> 12:22.075
Explain what?

12:23.159 --> 12:25.286
That you were still sincere?
That's so obvious.

12:26.663 --> 12:29.624
No matter what you say about it,
the truth won't change.

12:29.707 --> 12:31.501
Everything was fake from the start,

12:32.335 --> 12:34.545
and every moment you spent with me,

12:35.338 --> 12:37.257
you were hiding that secret from me.

12:38.716 --> 12:40.134
[♪ melancholy music playing]

12:40.218 --> 12:41.636
I knew it was too good to be true.

12:42.136 --> 12:44.430
There's no way
someone like me could be that happy.

12:45.098 --> 12:48.810
Whenever I feel like I'm really happy,

12:48.893 --> 12:49.978
I lose someone.

12:51.854 --> 12:52.855
[young Hadam] Hi!

12:52.939 --> 12:54.816
-[Hyewon] Hi.
-[Junho] They look so excited.

12:55.358 --> 12:56.359
[tires screech]

12:56.442 --> 12:57.819
Dad!

12:57.902 --> 12:59.153
[Haran] Mom and Dad, 13 years ago…

12:59.237 --> 13:00.613
[gasps, sighs]

13:00.697 --> 13:01.948
Just five minutes left.

13:02.031 --> 13:04.492
-[people clamoring]
-[siren blaring]

13:05.326 --> 13:06.619
[Haran] Hyeokchan, seven years ago…

13:07.287 --> 13:08.413
And today.

13:09.038 --> 13:10.832
You, Seonu Chan.

13:14.168 --> 13:16.379
This is the kind of ending that suits me.

13:17.005 --> 13:19.007
I'm not allowed to be happy.

13:20.425 --> 13:22.427
You've proven that once again.

13:23.136 --> 13:25.221
[breath trembling]

13:25.305 --> 13:26.306
Haran, please.

13:27.056 --> 13:28.433
If we end things like this,

13:29.017 --> 13:32.437
you'll go back
to putting up walls around you.

13:33.229 --> 13:35.356
-If you do that because of me--
-You're right.

13:36.399 --> 13:38.651
You just pushed me back into winter again.

13:39.527 --> 13:41.571
My past seven years, the present,

13:42.530 --> 13:43.865
and the future.

13:43.948 --> 13:44.949
[♪ music fades]

13:45.033 --> 13:46.701
You've ruined it all for me.

13:50.329 --> 13:52.165
[sighs] Just let me go.

13:53.499 --> 13:54.625
You disgust me.

14:05.136 --> 14:07.138
[♪ mellow song playing]

14:18.066 --> 14:20.068
[breathing heavily]

14:37.460 --> 14:38.795
[sharp inhale, groans]

14:41.422 --> 14:43.424
[sobbing]

14:52.016 --> 14:53.726
[sobbing]

15:00.525 --> 15:02.527
[Haran] Is it still valid?

15:02.610 --> 15:04.487
Being friends. The three-month trial.

15:04.570 --> 15:07.156
Then let's do this.
It'll be like we're on a spring picnic.

15:07.240 --> 15:08.241
Let's have fun.

15:08.324 --> 15:09.826
Ms. Song!

15:18.292 --> 15:20.670
You're Designer Song Haran, right?

15:21.504 --> 15:22.505
[Haran chuckles]

15:26.425 --> 15:28.344
[Chan] I'll wear this every day.

15:28.427 --> 15:30.179
[Haran shudders]

15:30.972 --> 15:31.973
[Haran chuckles]

15:33.099 --> 15:34.851
[Chan] I feel like I'm in a dream.

15:36.644 --> 15:37.812
[chuckles softly]

15:39.564 --> 15:40.982
[♪ song continues]

15:41.065 --> 15:43.734
[inaudible]

15:52.869 --> 15:54.745
[wind whooshes]

15:54.829 --> 15:57.790
-[leaves rustling]
-[birds chirping]

15:57.874 --> 15:59.792
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

15:59.876 --> 16:01.794
-[♪ song fades]
-[pens clatter]

16:04.046 --> 16:05.423
[objects clattering]

16:10.469 --> 16:11.470
SEONU CHAN

16:27.069 --> 16:28.154
[sighs]

16:31.616 --> 16:32.617
[sighs]

16:36.495 --> 16:38.497
[♪ soft emotional music playing]

16:59.644 --> 17:01.771
[Haran] I'm not allowed to be happy.

17:02.897 --> 17:04.649
You've proven that once again.

17:05.441 --> 17:07.652
You just pushed me back into winter again.

17:07.735 --> 17:10.529
My past seven years, the present,

17:10.613 --> 17:11.822
and the future.

17:11.906 --> 17:13.741
You've ruined it all for me.

17:14.951 --> 17:16.494
It's my fault…

17:19.997 --> 17:21.874
I have to do something.

17:24.335 --> 17:25.336
[exclaims softly]

17:26.379 --> 17:29.090
Talk it out with Haran.

17:29.173 --> 17:33.719
If you're sincere,
I'm sure she'll understand.

17:33.803 --> 17:35.221
[♪ music continues]

17:50.486 --> 17:51.487
[sighs]

17:58.953 --> 17:59.954
[♪ music fades]

18:00.037 --> 18:01.539
-[knocks on door]
-[Hayeong] Haran?

18:02.999 --> 18:04.542
What's going on?

18:04.625 --> 18:06.502
Why are you cooped up in here again?

18:07.086 --> 18:08.921
How is this scarf? Should I wear it?

18:10.256 --> 18:12.675
I'm heading to work in 10 minutes.
Do you want to…

18:15.845 --> 18:16.846
What?

18:17.805 --> 18:19.098
You're sweating.

18:20.933 --> 18:23.144
Haran, you're burning up.

18:24.145 --> 18:26.188
I told you to dress warmly, didn't I?

18:26.272 --> 18:28.774
-Let's go to the hospital.
-I can just take medicine.

18:28.858 --> 18:30.693
Medicine won't be enough right now.

18:31.444 --> 18:33.029
You should just rest today…

18:33.112 --> 18:35.573
How can I when Grandma's away?

18:36.157 --> 18:38.367
I'll get dressed, so get the car ready.

18:38.451 --> 18:39.702
[Hayeong sighs softly]

18:46.334 --> 18:48.085
Oh… Let's talk.

18:48.711 --> 18:51.339
[pants] I know you don't want to see me…

18:51.422 --> 18:53.382
[stutters] but just hear me out.

18:53.466 --> 18:57.053
If we end things like this,
you'll go back to how you used to be.

19:00.389 --> 19:01.390
All right.

19:02.224 --> 19:04.518
You don't have to look at me
or listen to me.

19:04.602 --> 19:07.104
So please, just look at this.

19:11.192 --> 19:13.819
-[Chan stutters]
-How many pills should you take?

19:13.903 --> 19:16.781
-Oh? It's Chan.
-Don't open the window. Just go.

19:17.281 --> 19:19.200
-But it's Chan.
-Just go.

19:19.909 --> 19:20.951
Okay.

19:25.665 --> 19:28.334
If he came all the way here,
it must be pretty important.

19:29.126 --> 19:31.045
What's going on? Did you have a fight?

19:32.004 --> 19:33.381
Let's just go quietly.

19:34.382 --> 19:37.176
He looks so down, though.

19:39.220 --> 19:40.429
[Hayeong sighs]

19:43.849 --> 19:45.851
Let's continue after lunch.

19:45.935 --> 19:48.229
-All right.
-[groans]

19:48.312 --> 19:49.897
[Haran] Can you--

19:49.980 --> 19:51.232
It's Chan.

19:51.315 --> 19:52.358
Hey, Chan.

20:00.408 --> 20:01.450
Ms. Song.

20:01.534 --> 20:03.119
I don't have any meetings today.

20:03.202 --> 20:04.578
Don't let anyone in.

20:05.204 --> 20:07.164
[Sol] Huh? But Chan…

20:07.665 --> 20:09.500
[Chan] I won't make any excuses.

20:09.583 --> 20:12.461
I know you don't want to listen,
so please…

20:12.545 --> 20:14.755
No exceptions.
Don't let anyone in my office.

20:25.182 --> 20:27.351
[♪ melancholy music playing]

20:27.435 --> 20:30.896
[hesitates] I'll buy lunch today.

20:31.480 --> 20:33.107
Why don't you join us since you're here?

20:33.733 --> 20:35.609
No, I'm okay.

20:38.904 --> 20:39.905
Ah.

20:40.406 --> 20:43.075
Please give this to her.
Don't tell her it's from me.

20:43.159 --> 20:44.368
[Raemee] Okay.

20:45.286 --> 20:47.121
He looks more sick than her, though.

20:58.048 --> 20:59.049
[sighs]

21:07.683 --> 21:08.684
[♪ music fades]

21:10.311 --> 21:12.104
Does this one stand out too much?

21:13.898 --> 21:15.983
[Seunggyu] It'll feel more like noise
than a focal point.

21:16.066 --> 21:17.318
What do you think?

21:17.943 --> 21:19.028
I agree.

21:19.111 --> 21:20.946
Then let's stick to the flow instead.

21:21.030 --> 21:22.323
-All right.
-Good.

21:23.532 --> 21:27.870
Oh. But has anyone
seen our robot, Mr. Yeon?

21:27.953 --> 21:31.248
I have to ask him
about our press cut deadline. [sighs]

21:31.332 --> 21:35.085
I haven't seen
his perfectly groomed hair for days.

21:35.169 --> 21:38.088
He must be incredibly busy
taking care of things for Ms. Kim.

21:38.172 --> 21:41.926
Right. He'll be busy
making up for her absence.

21:42.426 --> 21:45.471
But when did Mr. Yeon
start working in Nana Atelier?

21:46.305 --> 21:47.306
Since he was 19.

21:47.932 --> 21:48.933
[Seunggyu, Sol, and Raemee gasp]

21:49.016 --> 21:51.018
-Nineteen?
-[in English] Legend.

21:51.101 --> 21:52.812
[Sol exclaims, whines]

21:52.895 --> 21:56.232
[in Korean] But no matter how busy he is,
he does seem to have disappeared.

21:56.315 --> 21:58.442
-[Seunggyu] Mmm.
-Right.

21:58.943 --> 22:00.027
It's like he just quit.

22:00.110 --> 22:02.112
[Sol gasps] What if he really did?

22:02.780 --> 22:04.782
[♪ mellow music playing]

22:07.451 --> 22:10.371
[Sol] He could have,
if he's been working since he was 19.

22:12.623 --> 22:13.624
[♪ music fades]

22:14.250 --> 22:16.961
I organized the color differences
and confirmed the pigment.

22:17.044 --> 22:19.255
I also picked the other SS looks.

22:19.338 --> 22:21.549
And you need to approve this.

22:26.512 --> 22:28.013
How are you feeling?

22:30.975 --> 22:33.310
-I should ask the same thing.
-What?

22:33.394 --> 22:35.354
You look really unwell.

22:35.437 --> 22:38.691
-Oh… I just have a light cold.
-That's not all, is it?

22:39.942 --> 22:40.943
What is it?

22:41.026 --> 22:45.239
Has Mr. Seonu gotten worse?

22:46.240 --> 22:48.826
No, nothing's wrong. [chuckles awkwardly]

22:48.909 --> 22:52.580
Just focus on your condition
before your surgery.

22:52.663 --> 22:54.707
Don't worry about me or the company.

22:55.541 --> 22:58.168
Mr. Park, you can head home today.
I'll stay here.

22:58.252 --> 22:59.253
[Manjae] Mmm-mmm.

22:59.837 --> 23:02.590
I told you I'm in charge here.

23:02.673 --> 23:06.552
You should hurry home and rest.

23:06.635 --> 23:08.971
[Nana] You might end up
getting hospitalized instead of me.

23:09.054 --> 23:10.681
You look like you'll collapse.

23:10.764 --> 23:12.057
Go home.

23:12.516 --> 23:14.476
Then please take care of her.

23:15.352 --> 23:16.770
Thank you, Mr. Park.

23:17.521 --> 23:18.522
[in English] My pleasure.

23:18.606 --> 23:19.940
[chuckles]

23:20.024 --> 23:21.984
-[in Korean] Bye, then.
-Bye.

23:25.404 --> 23:27.031
It seems like something's up.

23:29.825 --> 23:31.869
Ms. Kim Nabong, worry about yourself

23:32.411 --> 23:35.039
until your surgery.

23:35.122 --> 23:36.123
Hmm?

23:42.379 --> 23:43.422
[therapist] Is this okay?

23:43.505 --> 23:44.590
Yes, it's okay.

23:44.673 --> 23:46.675
-Tell me if it hurts.
-Okay.

23:47.843 --> 23:49.845
[therapist]
You're checking with him again.

23:49.929 --> 23:52.014
Of course. I should record this every day.

23:52.097 --> 23:54.808
He has to pass
the medical test in February.

23:54.892 --> 23:56.727
Then let's check your ankle now.

23:56.810 --> 23:59.229
Try pulling with strength.

24:00.189 --> 24:01.732
[therapist inhales sharply]

24:01.815 --> 24:02.983
It doesn't hurt?

24:03.067 --> 24:04.652
No, not at all.

24:04.735 --> 24:08.280
[gasps] Your range of motion
has improved a lot since last week.

24:08.364 --> 24:09.448
Right, Doctor?

24:09.531 --> 24:11.075
[therapist] Yes. [chuckles]

24:11.158 --> 24:13.410
Then, next week,
we'll fit you with an ankle brace

24:13.494 --> 24:14.703
and work on standing up.

24:14.787 --> 24:16.914
Don't strain yourself. Good job.

24:16.997 --> 24:18.374
-Thank you.
-Bye.

24:19.375 --> 24:21.627
That was two degrees more than last week.

24:21.710 --> 24:23.504
Are you sure it didn't hurt?

24:23.587 --> 24:25.714
I know my body better than anyone.

24:25.798 --> 24:29.343
I feel like I'll be able to get up soon
and start throwing balls.

24:29.426 --> 24:30.928
[chuckles]

24:31.011 --> 24:34.181
Mr. Cha, you really have
exceptional recovery speed,

24:34.264 --> 24:35.683
-as expected.
-[clears throat]

24:35.766 --> 24:38.727
Then let's start
outdoors practice tomorrow

24:38.811 --> 24:40.980
so you don't lose your touch.

24:41.772 --> 24:44.274
Yes, Coach. Let's do this.

24:44.358 --> 24:45.359
[both chuckle]

24:45.442 --> 24:46.944
-[cell phone vibrating]
-Ah.

24:48.862 --> 24:50.155
-Hang on.
-Sure.

24:50.239 --> 24:51.490
Hello?

25:07.006 --> 25:08.048
Come in.

25:11.051 --> 25:12.636
Are you just going to leave again?

25:13.178 --> 25:14.471
Come in.

25:17.599 --> 25:18.684
Mr. Yeon.

25:42.916 --> 25:44.084
I've failed you again.

25:46.545 --> 25:49.173
I've never protected you properly.

25:50.466 --> 25:51.759
[breath trembling]

25:53.552 --> 25:54.595
I'm sorry.

25:54.678 --> 25:55.888
So,

25:58.057 --> 26:00.559
were you going to wait until I recovered

26:01.560 --> 26:02.770
and try to quit again?

26:03.562 --> 26:05.189
Like that day, 13 years ago?

26:05.272 --> 26:07.274
[♪ melancholy music playing]

26:10.694 --> 26:13.030
Good job. You can go now.

26:14.156 --> 26:15.657
Ms. Kim…

26:15.741 --> 26:18.160
LETTER OF RESIGNATION

26:18.243 --> 26:19.536
I'm sorry, Ms. Kim.

26:20.204 --> 26:21.955
If only I hadn't been sick that day…

26:23.040 --> 26:24.541
If I'd been the one driving…

26:26.710 --> 26:28.670
I couldn't even repay you
for your kindness.

26:29.129 --> 26:30.172
I'm sorry.

26:31.965 --> 26:34.510
If you have time to talk such nonsense,

26:35.052 --> 26:36.053
use that time

26:37.721 --> 26:38.972
to prepare for college.

26:40.766 --> 26:42.601
You'd better get accepted in one try.

26:43.769 --> 26:44.770
[♪ music fades]

26:46.230 --> 26:48.524
You made that same face

26:49.149 --> 26:51.193
after Hyewon and Junho's funeral.

26:55.989 --> 26:57.950
When I met you for the first time,

26:59.493 --> 27:01.954
do you know why I told you to come see me?

27:03.622 --> 27:05.082
You reminded me of my past.

27:06.542 --> 27:08.252
Even if no one noticed,

27:09.670 --> 27:11.296
I did my best

27:12.548 --> 27:15.884
and worked so hard on my own
in Paris when I was 20.

27:18.929 --> 27:20.889
[♪ sentimental music playing]

27:20.973 --> 27:22.474
As soon as I turned 20,

27:22.558 --> 27:24.977
I flew to Paris alone
with no friends or family.

27:25.060 --> 27:28.355
I threw myself
into both studying and love.

27:29.481 --> 27:31.191
But I suddenly got pregnant

27:31.775 --> 27:33.610
and gave birth by myself.

27:34.111 --> 27:35.571
I struggled so hard

27:36.572 --> 27:39.283
attending fashion school,
carrying a baby on my back.

27:43.662 --> 27:48.000
I told myself that someone
would notice my efforts someday,

27:49.418 --> 27:50.836
and I pushed through.

27:51.712 --> 27:52.796
[sobs]

27:52.880 --> 27:54.214
[Nana] Once I succeeded,

27:55.924 --> 27:57.009
I felt so much pity

27:58.594 --> 27:59.970
and pride

28:00.679 --> 28:02.264
for myself back then.

28:06.268 --> 28:07.603
I saw you that day,

28:08.729 --> 28:11.398
and I felt the same way about you.

28:12.733 --> 28:14.318
That's why I reached out a hand.

28:14.401 --> 28:17.821
Because I wanted to acknowledge
your efforts.

28:18.614 --> 28:19.615
You…

28:21.033 --> 28:22.367
took care of me…

28:25.329 --> 28:27.205
and changed my life, but…

28:27.289 --> 28:29.207
I never thought of it like that,

28:30.584 --> 28:32.669
but you've already repaid me enough.

28:32.753 --> 28:34.004
Without you,

28:34.087 --> 28:36.924
neither I nor my company nor my family

28:37.716 --> 28:39.885
would have gotten this far.

28:39.968 --> 28:41.053
No.

28:41.970 --> 28:42.971
I…

28:44.556 --> 28:46.308
I don't have the right to stay…

28:46.391 --> 28:47.768
Taeseok.

28:53.482 --> 28:54.775
Put down that burden now.

28:58.362 --> 29:00.364
You couldn't have prevented the accident

29:01.281 --> 29:02.616
by driving that day,

29:03.784 --> 29:05.494
nor could you have prevented this

29:06.411 --> 29:07.829
by noticing more quickly.

29:08.622 --> 29:11.500
No one in my family
blames you for what happened.

29:11.583 --> 29:14.544
You've been holding onto that guilt
because you're too kind.

29:16.004 --> 29:17.547
But you don't have to do that.

29:17.631 --> 29:19.800
-[sobbing]
-[Nana] Put it all down now.

29:25.847 --> 29:27.265
You've done a great job so far

29:28.266 --> 29:29.977
working by my side.

29:31.687 --> 29:34.815
So stay with me.

29:34.898 --> 29:37.693
[sobbing]

29:44.449 --> 29:46.451
[Taeseok crying]

29:54.835 --> 29:55.836
[young Hayeong] Mr. Yeon.

29:57.254 --> 29:58.505
[young Taeseok] I'm sorry.

29:58.588 --> 29:59.881
I'm really sorry.

29:59.965 --> 30:01.299
I'm sorry.

30:01.383 --> 30:02.843
I'm really sorry.

30:04.219 --> 30:05.220
I…

30:06.304 --> 30:07.973
shouldn't be sick.

30:11.935 --> 30:13.937
[Taeseok crying]

30:20.027 --> 30:22.029
[footsteps approaching]

30:22.112 --> 30:23.113
[♪ music ends]

30:29.578 --> 30:32.205
Do you want one?

30:41.339 --> 30:42.424
[Hayeong sighs]

30:45.135 --> 30:46.470
I'm sorry.

30:47.471 --> 30:49.222
I didn't mean to eavesdrop,

30:49.306 --> 30:53.685
but I brought fruits for Grandma
and ended up overhearing.

30:56.104 --> 30:59.900
Ah. So that's why
you were at Mom and Dad's grave.

30:59.983 --> 31:01.568
Okay. I understand now.

31:02.611 --> 31:05.197
-I'm sorry.
-Stop saying you're sorry.

31:05.280 --> 31:09.201
Like Grandma said,
none of us have ever blamed you.

31:09.284 --> 31:10.660
Not for a single second.

31:10.744 --> 31:13.205
Mom, Dad. It's not his fault, right?

31:15.749 --> 31:17.959
You heard that, right? They said no.

31:19.878 --> 31:20.879
[sighs softly]

31:24.049 --> 31:25.050
[Hayeong] Here.

31:25.133 --> 31:29.513
Have this sweet and sour candy
that you love so much…

31:34.351 --> 31:35.894
and leave all your burdens behind.

31:37.521 --> 31:38.939
[chuckles softly]

31:39.606 --> 31:40.607
Have this

31:41.650 --> 31:42.901
and cheer up.

31:46.530 --> 31:48.448
-You're giving this to me again.
-What?

31:48.990 --> 31:51.201
Didn't you give me one last time?

31:52.494 --> 31:53.578
Did I?

31:57.374 --> 32:00.168
[winces] It's so sour. Why is it so sour?

32:03.421 --> 32:04.631
[chuckles]

32:04.714 --> 32:06.716
[♪ heartwarming music playing]

32:07.592 --> 32:10.178
YOU SAVED ME TOO

32:13.265 --> 32:14.266
[Haran sighs]

32:15.183 --> 32:16.268
[Chan stutters]

32:16.351 --> 32:18.854
No exceptions.
Don't let anyone in my office.

32:23.733 --> 32:24.734
[sighs softly]

32:25.694 --> 32:27.529
[coughs, sniffles]

32:29.948 --> 32:32.576
[cell phone vibrating]

32:33.326 --> 32:35.036
MR. PARK

32:39.124 --> 32:40.125
Yes, Mr. Park.

32:40.792 --> 32:42.169
What's wrong with your voice?

32:42.252 --> 32:43.461
Did you catch a cold?

32:43.545 --> 32:44.546
Oh…

32:46.464 --> 32:49.134
Maybe it's because you're not here.
[chuckles softly]

32:49.217 --> 32:50.510
I have no one to talk to,

32:51.720 --> 32:54.931
so I guess my voice is a bit rusty.
[clears throat]

32:55.515 --> 32:57.934
[inhales sharply] Is…

32:59.019 --> 33:00.478
something the matter?

33:01.104 --> 33:03.607
Besides the fact that I miss you,
everything's fine.

33:04.399 --> 33:06.151
It must be tough at the hospital.

33:07.611 --> 33:10.238
I'm doing well here with Genius,

33:11.615 --> 33:12.657
so don't worry

33:13.658 --> 33:15.076
and take care of yourself, too.

33:15.744 --> 33:16.828
All right.

33:18.330 --> 33:19.414
[cell phone beeps]

33:21.583 --> 33:24.753
[Genius whining]

33:28.089 --> 33:29.299
I'm okay.

33:30.592 --> 33:33.678
No, I'll make sure everything's okay.

33:36.848 --> 33:38.850
Everything will be okay.

33:46.775 --> 33:48.109
Song Haran.

33:49.444 --> 33:50.445
[♪ music fades]

33:50.528 --> 33:51.947
You saved me,

33:52.697 --> 33:53.990
seven years ago.

33:54.658 --> 33:56.201
You saved me back then!

34:02.374 --> 34:03.500
[Chan panting]

34:05.794 --> 34:06.795
I'm sorry.

34:07.504 --> 34:09.339
Seven years ago and now,

34:09.422 --> 34:11.758
I've wanted to show you the real me.

34:13.426 --> 34:15.887
I should have told you, no matter what.

34:17.389 --> 34:18.431
[Chan sighs]

34:21.142 --> 34:22.269
It's all my fault.

34:26.898 --> 34:29.776
Please, just look at this.
Everything's in here.

34:30.902 --> 34:33.738
Stories that you don't know
about back then.

34:37.826 --> 34:39.160
Let me ask you two things.

34:40.912 --> 34:42.664
Just say yes or no.

34:46.126 --> 34:47.585
If I look at this,

34:49.713 --> 34:51.131
will it change the fact

34:53.300 --> 34:55.969
that you pretended to be Hyeokchan
and messaged me…

34:59.097 --> 35:00.098
seven years ago?

35:03.226 --> 35:05.395
[♪ melancholy music playing]

35:05.478 --> 35:07.022
-No.
-[Haran] Then,

35:07.105 --> 35:09.566
does it change the fact

35:11.651 --> 35:14.321
that you kept this secret from me
the whole time…

35:17.365 --> 35:18.450
while you were with me?

35:19.492 --> 35:21.661
-Haran.
-Say yes or no.

35:24.956 --> 35:25.957
No.

35:27.667 --> 35:29.669
-But--
-Then it won't change my mind.

35:31.254 --> 35:32.839
If those two facts don't change,

35:32.922 --> 35:35.091
then whatever explanation you give

35:36.259 --> 35:37.344
or whatever you do,

35:38.094 --> 35:39.471
it won't change my mind.

35:42.098 --> 35:46.186
If you still think the lies you told
can be explained by something,

35:47.812 --> 35:49.731
then you still have no clue

35:52.025 --> 35:53.902
how you've shattered my heart

35:55.737 --> 35:59.532
and how you've destroyed
the past seven years of my life.

36:01.993 --> 36:03.828
Don't ever show up in front of me again.

36:05.580 --> 36:06.790
When I see you,

36:08.333 --> 36:12.253
I feel like I'm going to lose my mind
thinking about the seven years I lost.

36:16.299 --> 36:18.134
[Chan] I won't even
think about staying with you.

36:18.218 --> 36:21.179
But you'll go back
to how you were seven years ago…

36:22.055 --> 36:23.139
[breath trembling]

36:27.477 --> 36:29.771
[high-pitched ringing]

36:29.854 --> 36:30.939
[groans]

36:32.899 --> 36:34.693
[groaning]

36:36.027 --> 36:37.028
[grunts]

36:37.112 --> 36:39.114
[breathing heavily]

36:57.090 --> 36:58.508
[♪ music swells]

37:20.363 --> 37:21.823
[♪ music fades]

37:21.906 --> 37:24.701
-[exclaims] Cha Yougyum!
-[clears throat]

37:24.784 --> 37:26.661
Your pitching is still amazing.

37:26.745 --> 37:31.416
No wonder you were always named MVP
at every tournament.

37:31.499 --> 37:32.584
[Hadam chuckles]

37:34.753 --> 37:35.754
[inhales sharply]

37:36.755 --> 37:37.756
[grunts]

37:38.715 --> 37:40.550
Oh, gosh, I missed it.

37:42.927 --> 37:44.179
[sighs softly]

37:45.972 --> 37:47.307
Hadam, let's stop.

37:47.390 --> 37:48.600
You must be tired.

37:48.683 --> 37:50.727
I'll ask Changmo to help me later.

37:50.810 --> 37:52.687
No. We can do it.

37:52.771 --> 37:54.063
Let's go.

37:55.648 --> 37:57.317
All right, throw it.

38:02.989 --> 38:04.324
[grunts]

38:04.407 --> 38:07.368
Gosh, I missed it again. I'll go get it.

38:14.876 --> 38:15.877
[sighs]

38:18.046 --> 38:19.214
[sighs worriedly]

38:23.134 --> 38:24.344
Did we overdo it?

38:25.094 --> 38:26.095
You must be tired.

38:26.846 --> 38:27.889
Not at all.

38:27.972 --> 38:29.474
I know my body best.

38:29.557 --> 38:31.601
[inhales sharply] I feel much lighter now.

38:33.353 --> 38:34.354
Oh, right.

38:35.605 --> 38:39.275
My team's visiting later,
so it's going to be really noisy.

38:39.359 --> 38:40.568
You should head home now.

38:40.652 --> 38:43.363
Then I should go and study rehabilitation.

38:44.405 --> 38:46.574
Have fun with the guys.
I'll call you later.

38:46.658 --> 38:47.742
Okay.

38:49.869 --> 38:51.496
[sighs dreamily]

38:52.080 --> 38:53.498
Those punks.

38:53.581 --> 38:56.292
I should give them some snacks.

38:57.126 --> 38:59.420
Hmm? It's pretty quiet, though.

39:03.007 --> 39:04.509
[Yougyum sobbing]

39:06.594 --> 39:08.555
[♪ emotional music playing]

39:08.638 --> 39:09.973
[umpire] Out!

39:10.056 --> 39:11.391
[players cheering]

39:11.474 --> 39:13.226
FINAL, CHEONGSOL HIGH 3
HANEUL HIGH 2

39:14.519 --> 39:15.520
[sniffles]

39:21.234 --> 39:22.944
[sniffles]

39:23.862 --> 39:25.321
[stutters] Yougyum.

39:27.699 --> 39:28.700
[Yougyum] Hadam…

39:30.326 --> 39:31.452
What do I do?

39:34.372 --> 39:35.915
[breathes shakily]

39:37.458 --> 39:38.459
I…

39:39.002 --> 39:40.795
I don't think I can make it.

39:42.839 --> 39:45.842
I know my body better than anyone.

39:47.218 --> 39:49.220
[Yougyum crying]

40:02.650 --> 40:05.320
CHEONGSOL HIGH SCHOOL WINS

40:11.409 --> 40:12.410
[♪ music fades]

40:17.457 --> 40:18.541
What is it?

40:19.542 --> 40:20.543
Can't you sleep?

40:21.002 --> 40:22.378
Should I turn the light off?

40:22.462 --> 40:23.463
No.

40:23.546 --> 40:24.547
Manjae,

40:25.381 --> 40:26.507
you should go home.

40:27.342 --> 40:28.718
Go and sleep comfortably.

40:30.428 --> 40:32.096
[Manjae] I'll go once you're asleep.

40:32.639 --> 40:34.140
But why can't you sleep?

40:37.268 --> 40:38.269
I just…

40:39.646 --> 40:41.481
have a lot on my mind.

40:42.357 --> 40:43.358
Goodness.

40:43.858 --> 40:45.068
It's snowing.

40:46.444 --> 40:48.363
[Manjae] Oh. It is.

40:54.994 --> 40:57.747
Why do you have a lot on your mind?

40:58.581 --> 41:02.835
You know I've been tough
since I was little, right?

41:04.170 --> 41:05.171
But…

41:06.589 --> 41:09.634
thinking about going under anesthesia
and getting surgery

41:11.469 --> 41:12.762
makes me feel a bit nervous.

41:18.101 --> 41:20.937
I'm sure the surgery will go well.

41:21.771 --> 41:24.899
Just be yourself, the strong Kim Nana,

41:26.025 --> 41:27.151
and get through this.

41:27.902 --> 41:32.073
I'm more worried about something else
than drilling a hole in my skull.

41:32.824 --> 41:33.825
What is it?

41:35.201 --> 41:36.953
I have to shave my head here.

41:37.787 --> 41:39.998
That would ruin my look.

41:40.498 --> 41:42.083
Why does that worry me more?

41:42.208 --> 41:44.502
[laughs]

41:44.585 --> 41:47.213
You really are the Chuncheon fashionista.

41:47.296 --> 41:48.548
[laughs]

41:50.550 --> 41:51.551
This won't do.

41:52.260 --> 41:55.388
I should protect your look.

41:56.264 --> 41:57.515
Hang on.

41:57.598 --> 41:58.725
What?

42:01.436 --> 42:02.437
Oh, my.

42:03.563 --> 42:05.440
This is hand-knitted.

42:06.482 --> 42:07.859
Did you really…

42:09.318 --> 42:11.320
[♪ lighthearted music playing]

42:13.406 --> 42:17.160
[Manjae] I knitted it in secret
while you were sleeping.

42:18.828 --> 42:22.206
But I think I'm a knitting genius.

42:23.291 --> 42:25.626
-I followed along easily.
-[gasps]

42:25.710 --> 42:27.086
I might have to open

42:27.712 --> 42:30.465
a knitting workshop in my coffee shop.

42:30.548 --> 42:31.716
-Huh?
-[chuckles]

42:31.799 --> 42:33.176
How did you…

42:33.259 --> 42:36.220
Would you like to try it on?

42:41.726 --> 42:42.727
Wow.

42:44.937 --> 42:46.147
You look beautiful.

42:46.230 --> 42:47.356
-Really?
-Yes.

42:47.440 --> 42:48.566
-Let me see.
-Okay.

42:50.777 --> 42:51.944
Here, look.

42:52.653 --> 42:54.197
[gasps, giggles]

42:57.492 --> 42:59.077
-[chuckles]
-Nabong.

42:59.827 --> 43:01.579
After the surgery,

43:04.082 --> 43:05.249
why don't you rest

43:06.459 --> 43:07.460
by my side?

43:08.836 --> 43:09.837
What?

43:09.921 --> 43:11.214
[Manjae] Kim Nabong.

43:12.340 --> 43:15.009
It took a long time,

43:16.135 --> 43:17.637
but will you begin

43:18.304 --> 43:20.765
your second "La Vie en Rose"

43:21.599 --> 43:23.643
with me, Park Manjae?

43:31.192 --> 43:32.401
Hmm?

43:33.444 --> 43:34.445
Manjae.

43:58.094 --> 44:00.763
You've been through so much all this time.

44:02.640 --> 44:04.016
So get some rest

44:05.476 --> 44:06.477
by my side now.

44:18.322 --> 44:19.323
[♪ music ends]

44:20.908 --> 44:22.034
Hey, roomie.

44:22.994 --> 44:24.912
Why are you sitting there in the dark?

44:32.170 --> 44:33.171
Hey.

44:33.838 --> 44:35.006
Is something wrong?

44:37.008 --> 44:38.050
She…

44:39.343 --> 44:40.887
found out about everything.

44:41.721 --> 44:43.556
I didn't have the chance to explain.

44:49.770 --> 44:51.397
It's all my fault,

44:52.440 --> 44:55.902
but she's the one suffering
when she did nothing wrong.

44:57.069 --> 44:58.946
It hurts so much

45:02.074 --> 45:03.659
to see her in pain…

45:05.453 --> 45:07.997
[scoffs] But I must be crazy.

45:09.999 --> 45:11.417
Despite everything,

45:14.921 --> 45:15.922
I still

45:17.632 --> 45:19.508
want to see her so badly.

45:21.302 --> 45:22.803
[Manjae sighs]

45:24.388 --> 45:26.224
If I lose her like this,

45:28.601 --> 45:29.894
if I…

45:31.896 --> 45:33.856
make her return to her old self,

45:35.107 --> 45:36.108
then…

45:37.235 --> 45:38.819
[sighs dejectedly] Then…

45:40.529 --> 45:42.073
Oh, dear…

45:43.616 --> 45:47.411
I did wonder if something was wrong. Gosh.

45:47.495 --> 45:48.579
[mumbles]

45:49.872 --> 45:50.873
[exclaims softly]

45:50.957 --> 45:51.958
You're burning up.

45:52.041 --> 45:53.584
How long have you been like this?

45:54.085 --> 45:56.087
-Huh? Oh?
-[Chan sighs]

45:56.170 --> 45:58.798
[exclaims worriedly] Hey! Roomie!

45:58.881 --> 45:59.924
Hey!

46:00.007 --> 46:01.092
Chan!

46:04.262 --> 46:05.680
Goodness.

46:12.270 --> 46:15.856
[Chan] I want to stay by her side

46:16.691 --> 46:19.026
in spring, in summer,

46:19.110 --> 46:20.736
in fall, and in winter.

46:21.487 --> 46:22.488
I want

46:22.571 --> 46:24.949
to stay by her side,

46:25.032 --> 46:26.909
but I don't know what to do.

46:26.993 --> 46:28.286
[♪ soft emotional music playing]

46:28.369 --> 46:31.289
Do you need someone to talk to?

46:32.248 --> 46:33.582
Ah…

46:33.666 --> 46:35.334
I made some assumptions,

46:36.002 --> 46:39.171
but there was a lot more I didn't know.

46:40.506 --> 46:43.301
You must have had
such a hard time until now.

46:44.135 --> 46:45.553
You've been through a lot.

46:46.554 --> 46:49.348
I want to tell her everything
and stay by her side,

46:50.057 --> 46:51.851
but if I tell her about myself,

46:54.270 --> 46:55.521
it will hurt her.

46:56.731 --> 46:58.607
I'm not even sure

46:58.691 --> 47:01.277
if I can explain myself to her
without reopening

47:01.861 --> 47:02.903
[sighs]

47:03.529 --> 47:04.655
her old wounds.

47:05.489 --> 47:07.283
But if you're this sincere,

47:07.867 --> 47:10.870
don't you think
she'll realize it in the end?

47:11.829 --> 47:14.290
To be honest, I'm scared.

47:15.624 --> 47:17.543
If I act rashly,

47:17.626 --> 47:20.671
my flawed memories might ruin everything.

47:21.255 --> 47:22.256
I'm scared…

47:25.676 --> 47:27.219
I'll hurt her again.

47:27.762 --> 47:28.804
Chan.

47:30.097 --> 47:31.807
After living all these years,

47:32.266 --> 47:35.144
what I've learned is that
waiting until everything's perfect

47:35.227 --> 47:37.021
isn't always the answer.

47:37.772 --> 47:40.191
For people and for love.

47:41.025 --> 47:42.276
[in Latin] "Memento Mori."

47:42.777 --> 47:44.320
[in Korean] You said
you don't want regrets.

47:44.904 --> 47:46.030
If you keep waiting,

47:46.113 --> 47:48.199
you might lose your chance
and regret it later.

47:48.282 --> 47:51.619
Why don't you show her
how sincere you are first?

47:52.536 --> 47:55.581
It won't be too late
to take care of other things later.

47:57.333 --> 47:58.751
[♪ music continues]

48:04.173 --> 48:07.927
[Chan] I should get ready
to explain myself to her.

48:10.346 --> 48:11.555
I should start

48:12.139 --> 48:14.058
by what happened seven years ago

48:16.769 --> 48:18.354
and tell her in my own way.

48:22.608 --> 48:23.609
[♪ music fades]

48:23.692 --> 48:25.444
[shudders] It's so cold.

48:25.528 --> 48:28.614
Why are you brooding out here in the cold?

48:28.697 --> 48:30.157
What time is it?

48:30.241 --> 48:31.575
[Hayeong] It's past midnight.

48:31.659 --> 48:33.953
How long have you been here?
You're already unwell.

48:34.036 --> 48:35.037
Come inside.

48:35.996 --> 48:38.207
Oh, uh… Did you go to the hospital?

48:40.209 --> 48:42.169
Haran, what is it?

48:42.920 --> 48:44.839
Huh? Is something wrong?

48:45.506 --> 48:46.799
What's going on?

48:47.383 --> 48:49.135
-Hayeong.
-Yes?

48:50.636 --> 48:51.971
I want to wake up.

48:54.723 --> 48:57.268
I thought I was in a dream until now,

48:58.644 --> 49:00.229
but I guess it was a nightmare.

49:01.605 --> 49:02.940
[♪ somber music playing]

49:03.023 --> 49:04.900
I want to wake up,

49:06.110 --> 49:07.820
but I don't know how.

49:09.780 --> 49:13.284
-Haran.
-We're not meant to be together.

49:15.619 --> 49:18.998
I have to forget things
that seem impossible to forget.

49:22.084 --> 49:23.461
But I don't know

49:25.087 --> 49:27.173
how to get over everything.

49:29.592 --> 49:30.593
[Hayeong sighs softly]

49:34.221 --> 49:35.514
[sighs]

49:41.228 --> 49:43.147
-[ice cubes clacking]
-[Hayeong sighs]

49:44.356 --> 49:45.566
[Hayeong grunts softly]

49:49.153 --> 49:50.154
[thermometer beeps]

49:51.697 --> 49:54.283
[sighs in relief] Her fever dropped.

49:56.702 --> 49:58.204
Gosh…

50:03.626 --> 50:04.627
[grunts softly]

50:06.003 --> 50:07.004
[♪ music fades]

50:07.087 --> 50:08.130
What?

50:09.673 --> 50:11.717
Gosh. What time is it?

50:11.800 --> 50:13.928
0202
NOV 29 SAT

50:14.637 --> 50:15.763
Are you here?

50:16.889 --> 50:17.890
What?

50:19.099 --> 50:20.267
Where did she go?

50:21.894 --> 50:22.937
Haran!

50:24.855 --> 50:26.941
-[sighs wearily]
-[line connects, ringing]

50:27.024 --> 50:29.109
[cell phone vibrating]

50:30.444 --> 50:32.279
HAYEONG

50:34.031 --> 50:35.824
[panting] What?

50:37.868 --> 50:39.411
Where did she go?

50:45.751 --> 50:46.752
[cell phone vibrating]

50:46.835 --> 50:48.087
DESIGNER SONG HAYEONG

50:48.671 --> 50:50.673
[breathing heavily]

50:51.173 --> 50:52.174
[grunts]

50:52.800 --> 50:54.802
[cell phone continues vibrating]

50:56.929 --> 50:58.264
[groans softly]

50:58.973 --> 51:00.099
[sighing]

51:07.064 --> 51:08.941
[groans softly] Hey, Hayeong.

51:09.024 --> 51:11.902
Chan, sorry to call you so late.

51:12.611 --> 51:14.321
But did Haran contact you?

51:16.073 --> 51:18.867
[grunts] Why? What's wrong?

51:18.951 --> 51:21.203
Haran's gone.

51:21.287 --> 51:24.164
The car's gone,
but she's not at the office either.

51:24.248 --> 51:28.085
You're the only one
I could ask where she could be.

51:29.211 --> 51:31.964
I feel so anxious after what she said.

51:32.047 --> 51:36.176
She said she was in a dream,
but it was a nightmare.

51:36.885 --> 51:37.886
[breath trembling]

51:39.555 --> 51:41.015
[♪ tense music playing]

51:41.098 --> 51:43.225
-I think I know where she is.
-[Manjae exclaims worriedly]

51:43.309 --> 51:45.269
Where are you going?
You're still burning up.

51:45.352 --> 51:47.187
I have to go find her.

51:48.063 --> 51:49.064
It has to be me.

51:49.148 --> 51:52.067
[stutters] What are you saying?
Did something happen to Haran?

51:53.152 --> 51:54.737
Huh? Chan!

51:55.195 --> 51:56.614
[♪ music continues]

52:01.035 --> 52:02.995
[Hayeong] She said
you're not meant to be together

52:03.704 --> 52:05.331
and that she has to forget it.

52:05.414 --> 52:08.208
I couldn't understand what she was saying,

52:08.792 --> 52:10.961
but she's really sick right now.

52:12.087 --> 52:13.714
[Chan] I feel like I'm in a dream.

52:13.797 --> 52:16.842
[Haran] Those words sounded a bit sad.

52:17.384 --> 52:20.512
It sounds like
they're not meant to be together.

52:21.138 --> 52:23.349
-[engine revving]
-[navigator beeping]

52:23.432 --> 52:25.434
[breathing shakily]

52:36.695 --> 52:40.115
[Haran] I said I won't ever forget

52:40.199 --> 52:42.242
this moment.

52:42.326 --> 52:44.912
Ah, and in spring…

52:44.995 --> 52:47.623
[Chan] Let's go see
the cherry blossoms in spring.

52:47.706 --> 52:49.833
We'll have shaved ice in summer…

52:50.584 --> 52:52.878
Oh, and go to the beach.

52:53.796 --> 52:55.631
We'll see the autumn leaves in fall,

52:56.131 --> 52:59.009
and in winter,
it would be fun to go snowboarding.

53:03.013 --> 53:04.014
[♪ music fades]

53:04.098 --> 53:05.891
-[engine revving]
-[navigator beeping]

53:09.728 --> 53:10.813
[breathing heavily]

53:10.896 --> 53:12.815
[♪ foreboding music playing]

53:14.274 --> 53:15.275
[grunts]

53:15.359 --> 53:18.445
-[high-pitched ringing]
-[grunts]

53:18.529 --> 53:20.030
[Hyeokchan] Do you have any idea
what you've done?

53:20.114 --> 53:22.116
-[Sujin] You must've jumped at the chance.
-[Haran] I love you, Chan.

53:22.199 --> 53:23.534
Kang Hyeokchan.

53:23.617 --> 53:24.952
Did you have fun…

53:25.953 --> 53:28.288
[grunts, exhales heavily]

53:30.207 --> 53:32.251
[high-pitched ringing]

53:40.134 --> 53:41.135
[♪ music fades]

53:41.552 --> 53:43.387
[tires screech]

53:44.471 --> 53:46.473
[Chan breathing heavily]

53:47.850 --> 53:49.852
[♪ pensive music playing]

54:09.037 --> 54:12.666
HADONGDO-GIL

54:12.750 --> 54:14.752
[breathing heavily]

54:17.087 --> 54:18.172
No…

54:19.423 --> 54:20.424
No…

54:20.924 --> 54:22.217
Please…

54:22.301 --> 54:24.595
[♪ dramatic music playing]

54:24.678 --> 54:25.846
It can't be…

54:26.430 --> 54:27.806
No way…

54:27.890 --> 54:28.891
Please…

54:30.309 --> 54:31.894
There is no way I caused it.

54:37.441 --> 54:38.942
[Haran crying]

54:47.367 --> 54:48.827
[Chan] But what if I did?

54:50.204 --> 54:51.288
Then she…

54:51.371 --> 54:52.789
[♪ music swells]

54:54.333 --> 54:56.335
[Haran bawling]

54:58.086 --> 55:00.088
[inaudible]

55:19.983 --> 55:22.402
-[♪ music fades]
-[PA beeps]

55:23.070 --> 55:25.072
[indistinct announcement on PA]

55:35.916 --> 55:37.209
[sighs]

55:39.002 --> 55:40.087
I wanted…

55:43.298 --> 55:45.008
to check something for the last time.

55:46.343 --> 55:47.886
Seven years ago…

55:47.970 --> 55:49.429
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

55:49.513 --> 55:50.764
…on the day of the accident.

55:52.641 --> 55:53.684
Did I…

55:55.769 --> 55:57.104
hit Kang Hyeokchan?

55:58.772 --> 56:01.984
Did I hit him and make him fall down?

56:03.360 --> 56:04.570
Is that why his lip tore

56:05.112 --> 56:06.822
and the waste container fell down?

56:11.159 --> 56:12.244
Is that true?

56:13.120 --> 56:14.121
Yes.

56:16.540 --> 56:18.125
You hit Hyeokchan.

56:21.753 --> 56:23.839
But why?

56:23.922 --> 56:24.923
[Sujin] Don't you remember?

56:25.007 --> 56:29.094
The day he came back from his trip,
you told Hyeokchan everything.

56:31.138 --> 56:32.139
[door closes]

56:34.433 --> 56:35.434
[♪ music fades]

56:35.517 --> 56:36.893
Long time no see.

56:37.477 --> 56:39.229
-Right.
-Hang on.

56:42.608 --> 56:46.320
[sighs] Sorry about this.
We need to switch laptops back.

56:46.403 --> 56:48.405
Move all your data from my laptop.

56:49.281 --> 56:50.282
Oh…

56:50.365 --> 56:51.366
Well…

56:52.326 --> 56:53.410
I…

56:53.493 --> 56:55.037
I have something to tell you.

56:56.163 --> 56:58.498
You do? What is it?

56:59.082 --> 57:00.334
[Chan] Uh…

57:03.003 --> 57:04.838
While you were away, I--

57:04.921 --> 57:06.715
Will this take long?

57:07.966 --> 57:09.343
Yes, a bit.

57:09.426 --> 57:10.886
Then let's talk later.

57:10.969 --> 57:12.888
I have to meet my professor right now.

57:13.430 --> 57:15.015
I'll see you, uh…

57:15.849 --> 57:17.351
in the lab later.

57:22.939 --> 57:23.940
[sighs softly]

57:24.316 --> 57:25.859
Right. What is it?

57:26.443 --> 57:27.944
You needed to tell me something.

57:28.028 --> 57:29.196
Your messenger…

57:29.946 --> 57:31.114
What?

57:32.240 --> 57:34.117
While I was using your laptop,

57:34.993 --> 57:38.121
I kept chatting with your girlfriend.

57:42.793 --> 57:43.919
What?

57:44.002 --> 57:45.671
[♪ tense music playing]

57:45.754 --> 57:48.382
What are you talking about?
Say that again.

57:48.465 --> 57:49.925
We ended up

57:50.967 --> 57:52.344
chatting after that.

57:53.512 --> 57:56.014
But she thinks it was you.

57:57.724 --> 58:00.560
[chuckling] Hyeokchan,
you left your earphones in my car…

58:01.144 --> 58:02.187
[Hyeokchan] Are you saying

58:02.771 --> 58:05.357
you've been talking to Haran

58:06.233 --> 58:07.484
while I was away?

58:07.943 --> 58:08.944
Pretending to be me?

58:14.032 --> 58:15.659
Sorry. It's all my fault.

58:16.576 --> 58:17.577
[sighs]

58:19.079 --> 58:20.080
Hang on. [sighs]

58:21.748 --> 58:22.999
Who are you to do that?

58:23.875 --> 58:27.671
Why would you ruin everything like this?

58:28.255 --> 58:31.675
Tell me. What sort of things
have you been saying?

58:32.259 --> 58:33.260
Why?

58:33.343 --> 58:35.887
Did you think it was okay
since I asked you a few times?

58:35.971 --> 58:38.390
You were someone nobody even cared about.

58:39.725 --> 58:43.145
Did you get excited
that someone paid attention to you?

58:43.228 --> 58:44.813
[Chan grunts]

58:44.896 --> 58:46.857
-Kang Hyeokchan!
-[groans softly]

58:46.940 --> 58:50.861
[Sujin] You had your eye
on Hyeokchan's girlfriend, Song Haran.

58:51.820 --> 58:53.155
You told him

58:53.697 --> 58:56.825
that you'd been chatting with her
while he was traveling,

58:56.908 --> 58:58.410
so things got heated.

58:59.119 --> 59:00.704
And you ended up hitting him.

59:00.787 --> 59:02.122
[breath trembling]

59:03.457 --> 59:06.626
Can you still say
you didn't have feelings for her then?

59:06.710 --> 59:08.712
[♪ dramatic music playing]

59:09.379 --> 59:10.422
Then…

59:12.299 --> 59:14.885
[breath trembling] that accident…

59:16.011 --> 59:18.221
Was it because of the container that fell?

59:18.305 --> 59:20.307
[Sujin] Yes. So how do you feel?

59:20.891 --> 59:23.351
Does it feel good to know the truth?

59:25.604 --> 59:26.855
I told you,

59:26.938 --> 59:29.357
nothing good would come
from digging up the past.

59:34.070 --> 59:36.740
It was all because of you.

59:37.824 --> 59:39.242
You caused the accident,

59:39.326 --> 59:42.287
and it killed Hyeokchan
and hurt a lot of people.

59:49.127 --> 59:51.213
Don't act like it's some grand love story.

59:51.296 --> 59:54.549
You just tried to steal
Hyeokchan's girlfriend

59:54.633 --> 59:57.093
and caused the accident that killed him.

59:57.177 --> 59:58.595
That's all you are.

59:58.678 --> 01:00:00.096
[♪ music swells]

01:00:02.307 --> 01:00:04.142
Do you have any idea what you've done?

01:00:04.559 --> 01:00:06.228
I'm sorry. It's all my fault.

01:00:09.815 --> 01:00:13.068
It was all my fault.

01:00:19.908 --> 01:00:21.451
[♪ music fades]

01:00:21.535 --> 01:00:24.412
Where in the world did you go?
You even left your phone behind.

01:00:24.496 --> 01:00:26.873
You think I wouldn't worry
if you disappeared like that?

01:00:29.042 --> 01:00:30.252
[Hayeong clicks tongue]

01:00:31.711 --> 01:00:32.838
I was so worried.

01:00:32.921 --> 01:00:35.090
You'd better not do that again.

01:00:35.173 --> 01:00:36.967
I'm sorry for making you worry.

01:00:38.718 --> 01:00:40.929
Ah. What about Chan?

01:00:41.972 --> 01:00:43.932
Don't even mention him to me anymore.

01:00:44.015 --> 01:00:46.893
I mean, didn't you meet him?

01:00:47.519 --> 01:00:51.064
He heard you were gone
and started his car right away.

01:00:51.147 --> 01:00:53.108
-Didn't you see him?
-What do you mean?

01:00:53.191 --> 01:00:57.404
I called him late last night
because I didn't know where you were.

01:00:57.487 --> 01:00:59.364
-I thought he might know.
-[sighs]

01:00:59.447 --> 01:01:02.951
He said he knew where you could be
and left right away.

01:01:03.535 --> 01:01:04.828
Maybe you missed each other.

01:01:04.911 --> 01:01:06.997
Don't contact him about me anymore.

01:01:07.664 --> 01:01:09.124
He has nothing to do with me.

01:01:13.712 --> 01:01:15.213
His phone's off.

01:01:17.841 --> 01:01:18.842
[sighs]

01:01:20.594 --> 01:01:22.387
[Chan] I couldn't react properly.

01:01:22.470 --> 01:01:24.139
-[car honk echoes]
-[high-pitched ringing]

01:01:24.472 --> 01:01:26.600
It's hard to tell
where sounds are coming from.

01:01:27.642 --> 01:01:28.643
[sighs]

01:01:32.606 --> 01:01:34.357
What is it? Where are you going?

01:01:35.400 --> 01:01:36.860
Where are you going?

01:01:36.943 --> 01:01:39.237
This patient was transferred

01:01:39.321 --> 01:01:41.907
after a lab explosion in Boston
seven years ago.

01:01:41.990 --> 01:01:43.617
He was treated for full-body burns,

01:01:43.700 --> 01:01:46.578
and shrapnel is still lodged deep
in the temporal bone.

01:01:47.162 --> 01:01:50.457
It's a high-risk area, so we are only
monitoring it at the moment.

01:01:50.540 --> 01:01:52.876
He also has unilateral hearing loss.

01:01:52.959 --> 01:01:54.419
Burns? Shrapnel?

01:01:54.502 --> 01:01:57.589
He visited the ER recently
after a brief loss of consciousness

01:01:57.672 --> 01:01:59.090
and minor bleeding.

01:01:59.174 --> 01:02:02.427
The outpatient clinic will check
if it's related to the shrapnel.

01:02:02.510 --> 01:02:04.429
That really is a difficult spot.

01:02:04.512 --> 01:02:05.555
[presenter] That's right.

01:02:05.639 --> 01:02:08.224
If his bleeding
was caused by the shrapnel,

01:02:08.308 --> 01:02:10.018
it may be accompanied

01:02:10.101 --> 01:02:13.021
by neurological symptoms
such as auditory or visual hallucinations.

01:02:13.104 --> 01:02:15.315
There have even been reports
of memory distortion

01:02:15.398 --> 01:02:17.275
in severe cases like this.

01:02:17.359 --> 01:02:19.486
[♪ pensive music playing]

01:02:19.569 --> 01:02:22.113
The patient with the shrapnel
in the temporal bone…

01:02:22.197 --> 01:02:23.365
Did he take the exam?

01:02:23.949 --> 01:02:26.368
No, it's past his appointment,
but he hasn't shown up.

01:02:27.911 --> 01:02:28.912
But why do you ask?

01:02:28.995 --> 01:02:30.121
SEONU CHAN

01:02:33.333 --> 01:02:34.459
It's nothing.

01:02:34.960 --> 01:02:35.961
[♪ music fades]

01:02:36.044 --> 01:02:37.379
Mr. Park.

01:02:37.963 --> 01:02:39.547
Mr. Park, did you see…

01:02:41.883 --> 01:02:42.884
[sighs]

01:02:44.010 --> 01:02:46.012
[♪ soft emotional music playing]

01:03:04.990 --> 01:03:06.199
[Chan] A three-month trial!

01:03:06.282 --> 01:03:07.742
Just try me out as a free trial.

01:03:07.826 --> 01:03:12.497
As soon as the three months are over,
I'll disappear without a trace.

01:03:13.873 --> 01:03:15.125
[breathing heavily]

01:03:19.879 --> 01:03:23.925
END OF TRIAL

01:03:33.601 --> 01:03:34.602
[♪ music ends]

01:03:36.271 --> 01:03:38.481
We can proceed
with the model fitting as revised.

01:03:38.565 --> 01:03:40.066
[Raemee] Spring is here!

01:03:40.150 --> 01:03:41.568
Spring is here!

01:03:41.651 --> 01:03:42.819
Spring is here!

01:03:42.902 --> 01:03:44.446
Look, spring is here.

01:03:44.946 --> 01:03:47.782
-The forsythias have started blooming.
-[Hayeong gasps]

01:03:48.241 --> 01:03:50.201
The forsythias are blooming?

01:03:50.285 --> 01:03:52.412
That means we're on a tight schedule.

01:03:52.495 --> 01:03:54.789
All right, let's hang in there
for a few more days.

01:03:54.873 --> 01:03:55.999
-Let's do this!
-Let's do this!

01:03:56.082 --> 01:03:58.835
-Let's do this!
-I'm so sleepy.

01:03:58.918 --> 01:04:00.420
-[Sol chuckles]
-[Raemee] Goodness.

01:04:00.503 --> 01:04:02.505
[pen scraping]

01:04:05.341 --> 01:04:08.887
[Haran] The seasons of life
don't come in order.

01:04:14.225 --> 01:04:15.226
[sighs softly]

01:04:15.977 --> 01:04:17.437
It really is spring.

01:04:20.482 --> 01:04:22.400
Sometimes, when you think it's spring,

01:04:24.277 --> 01:04:26.196
winter suddenly arrives.

01:04:31.576 --> 01:04:32.577
Take this.

01:04:33.369 --> 01:04:34.370
Oh…

01:04:35.371 --> 01:04:36.748
Then let's do this.

01:04:36.831 --> 01:04:38.625
It'll be like we're on a spring picnic.

01:04:39.501 --> 01:04:40.502
Let's have fun.

01:04:42.587 --> 01:04:43.671
[♪ soft emotional song playing]

01:05:09.572 --> 01:05:12.325
SUMMER, SEVEN YEARS AGO
IT STARTED WITH WALLS

01:05:15.411 --> 01:05:17.413
END OF TRIAL

01:05:19.499 --> 01:05:21.459
[Haran] The man

01:05:22.127 --> 01:05:24.587
who suddenly lit up
my cold winter last year

01:05:24.671 --> 01:05:26.339
like radiant spring sunlight…

01:05:27.382 --> 01:05:30.218
disappeared from my life.

01:05:55.743 --> 01:05:57.453
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

01:06:21.561 --> 01:06:23.688
[Haran] He disappeared.

01:06:23.771 --> 01:06:27.150
The Seonu Chan I know
would never leave like this.

01:06:27.734 --> 01:06:29.027
[Sujin] He disappeared because of me.

01:06:29.110 --> 01:06:31.321
-I did something I shouldn't have.
-[bracelet clinks]

01:06:31.404 --> 01:06:33.406
He's been preparing for a long time.

01:06:33.489 --> 01:06:36.492
It's gotten so bad
that there's nothing they can do.

01:06:36.576 --> 01:06:37.911
-[Chan] Do you remember…
-[Haran cries]

01:06:37.994 --> 01:06:41.664
…how I was trapped in winter for so long?

01:06:41.748 --> 01:06:43.583
I knew you'd understand

01:06:44.876 --> 01:06:46.461
my sincerity.

01:06:46.544 --> 01:06:48.630
[Haran] Seonu Chan, where are you?

01:06:48.713 --> 01:06:50.882
Where on earth are you?

01:06:53.968 --> 01:06:54.969
[♪ song fades]

01:06:55.094 --> 01:06:57.096
[♪ theme music playing]

01:07:02.936 --> 01:07:03.937
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

01:07:04.020 --> 01:07:05.021
Translated by Juyoung Park
